{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden fixture for computeGoalProgress, shared between app/src/goals/goalProgress.ts",
    "and website/js/goals.js -- two independent implementations of the same",
    "window/progress math (see each file's own header for why they can't import",
    "one another). Lives under tests/fixtures/ (not app/src/goals/ or website/js/)",
    "because it's read by BOTH suites and neither owns the other's directory.",
    "",
    "Every `expected` array was produced by RUNNING the real website/js/goals.js",
    "computeGoalProgress (the two implementations are formula-identical), then",
    "verified by hand against the window/topic/met semantics documented in",
    "goalProgress.ts's own comments -- not just checked for agreement between the",
    "two sides. nowMs values are epoch ms produced by",
    "`new Date(2024, 0, 10, 12, 0, 0)` (a Wednesday) and",
    "`new Date(2024, 11, 15, 12, 0, 0)` in this repo's local timezone, same",
    "convention as goalProgress.test.ts/tests/website/goals.test.js's own NOW.",
    "",
    "If you change the window/progress math on EITHER side, this fixture stops",
    "being a safe oracle -- regenerate it (see goalProgress.golden.test.ts's",
    "header for the regeneration recipe) and re-verify by inspection, don't just",
    "silence the failing assertions.",
    "",
    "A goal with targetS <= 0 IS covered (nonpositive_target_guards_the_divide).",
    "It used to be excluded, because the two sides disagreed: goalProgress.ts",
    "guarded the divide and returned 0, while website/js/goals.js divided bare",
    "and produced NaN/Infinity. The website now carries the same guard, so the",
    "case is asserted rather than merely documented. It is unreachable through",
    "createGoal/updateGoal or sanitizeRemoteGoals, which both enforce",
    "targetS >= MIN_TARGET_S -- but it is the shape a corrupted or hand-built",
    "synced goal takes, which is why the app guarded it in the first place."
  ],
